My oldest surviving UseNet post is from 1983.  I
am eyewitness to that past.  One part of your
statement is wrong, though.  Policing was remarkably
absent when it comes to format.  Before the first
big dial-in ISP connected, there isn't a single
top-post to be found in the entire history of
UseNet.  Until non-professionals arrived no one even
thought to put responses before the earlier text
Jeopardy style.  No one failed to trim posts.
Folks couldn't even unsub from news.announce.newuser
so everyone at least skimmed the rules.  There are
many occurances of policing about advertizing.  So
the policing was there but what was policed was
different.

